        "previousSay": "The three totals fill the migrate row first. Then the other query/key pairs fill the same grid. Each snippet keeps its own batch, while the query and key axes give three by three scores; the full output shape is two by three by three. Matrix multiplication, the at-sign operation, needs the key matrix transposed on its last two axes. The shared feature axis disappears into each dot product. Elementwise multiplication would compare only matching token positions."
